          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#differential_orientation Differential orientation
          %p
            The operation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration"} fiber integration
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology
            requires a choice of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation+in+generalized+cohomology"} orientation in generalized cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            this is to be refined to a
            %em differential orientation
            \.
          %p
            Accordingly, instead of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+class"} Thom class
            there is a
            %em differential Thom class
            \.
          #DifferentialThomCocycle.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \to X
              a smooth real
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank"} rank
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              a
              %strong differential Thom cocycle
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+support"} compactly supported
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat \omega
                  in the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
                  of degree
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  of
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi V
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %li
                %p
                  such that for each
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
                  we have
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ∫
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi V
                              %mi x
                        %mi ω
                        %mo =
                        %mo ±
                        %mn 1
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\int_{V_x} \omega = \pm 1
                        \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The underlying class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mover
                      %mi ω
