          %p (…)
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+parallel+transport"}> higher parallel transport
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+holonomy"} higher holonomy
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration+in+differential+K-theory"} fiber integration in differential K-theory
          %h2#References References
          %p
            A discussion in the general sense of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration"} fiber integration
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology
            is in section 3.4 of
          %ul
            %li#HopkinsSinger
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Hopkins"}> Mike Hopkins
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isadore+Singer"} Isadore Singer
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quadratic+Functions+in+Geometry%2C+Topology%2Cand+M-Theory"} Quadratic Functions in Geometry, Topology,and M-Theory
          %p
            and around prop. 2.1 (in the context of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
              ,
              %em Classical Chern-Simons theory
              II. Special issue for S. S. Chern. Houston J. Math. 28 (2002), no. 2, 293–310.
          %p
            Explicit formulas for fiber integration of
            %em cocycles
            in
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+cohomology"} Deligne cohomology
            are given in
          %ul
            %li#GomiTerashima00
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kiyonori+Gomi"} Kiyonori Gomi
              and Yuji Terashima,
              %em A Fiber Integration Formula for the Smooth Deligne Cohomology
              International Mathematics Research Notices 2000, No. 13 (
              %a{:href => "http://imrn.oxfordjournals.org/content/2000/13/699.full.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://numr.wdfiles.com/local--files/differential-cohomology/gomi-terashima.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and their generalization from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+holonomy"} higher holonomy
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+parallel+transport"} higher parallel transport
            in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kiyonori+Gomi"} Kiyonori Gomi
              and Yuji Terashima,
              %em Higher dimensional parallel transport
              Mathematical Research Letters 8, 25–33 (2001) (
              %a{:href => "http://intlpress.com/_newsite/site/pub/files/_fulltext/journals/mrl/2001/0008/0001/MRL-2001-0008-0001-A-004.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p and
          %ul
            %li
              David Lipsky,
              %em Cocycle constructions for topological field theories
              (2010) (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/LipskyThesis.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Johan+Dupont"}> Johan Dupont
              , Rune Ljungmann,
              %em Integration of simplicial forms and Deligne cohomology
              Math. Scand. 97 (2005), 11–39 (
              %a{:href => "http://www.mscand.dk/article.php?id=897"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            The observation that the construction in
            %a{:href => "#GomiTerashima00"} Gomi-Terashima 00
            induces refines to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid"} smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+infinity-stack"} higher moduli stacks
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#FiorenzaSatiSchreiber12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Extended+higher+cup-product+Chern-Simons+theories"} Extended higher cup-product Chern-Simons theories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1207.5449"} arXiv:1207.5449
          %p for the case without boundary and for the general case in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              et al.
